  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A beam of monochromatic blue light is incident on a metal surface and as a result, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"N\"></span> electrons are emitted from the surface per second. The momentum of each electron is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"p\"></span>. What happens to the  number of electrons emitted per second and to the momentum of the electrons when the colour of the light is changed to orange, while the intensity of the light is kept constant?</p>\n\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Number of emitted electrons per second</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Momentum of the emitted electrons</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"A\">\n<td><strong>A.</strong></td>\n<td>Larger than <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"N\"></span></td>\n<td>Smaller than <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"p\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"B\">\n<td><strong>B.</strong></td>\n<td>Larger than <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"N\"></span></td>\n<td>Larger than <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"p\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"C\">\n<td><strong>C.</strong></td>\n<td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"N\"></span></td>\n<td>Smaller than <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"p\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"D\">\n<td><strong>D.</strong></td>\n<td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"N\"></span></td>\n<td>Larger than <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"p\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
  },
